    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** Students are building a vocabulary of HTML elements so they can name what they want when prompting AI. The goal is not mastery of HTML or even writing any code yourself \\- it's fluency enough to direct AI precisely. \r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What did you learn about this element? Can you explain it in your own words?\"  \r\n- \"How did you describe it in your prompt? What specific language did you use?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may use vague prompts like \"add a list\" without specifying content \\- ask them \"what should the list say?\"  \r\n- Students may not understand why the element matters for their own page \\- connect it explicitly: \"where could you use this on the page you built in Act 1?\"",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
